    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. ruby.py:3450-3476: when the typed receiver's class does not declare the method, callee is None and the branch falls through silently. `k = Kid.new; k.hello` with hello inherited from Base emits nothing end to end; `k.missing` also emits nothing, where an untyped receiver gets the external placeholder. The common real shape is `user = User.new; user.save`. The external-class half is WI-fanad. r15, v05."  # ed0e
